BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Old Fort Fifty
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270814
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270814
DTSTAMP:20261126T190045Z
UID:574c90ce85701ccd@altar.bike
CATEGORIES:race
DESCRIPTION:The Old Fort Fifty will be held on the rugged\, legendary trai
 ls that have made the area famous in the mountain bike world while also in
 corporating some newer trails recently built by the G5 Trail Collective. W
 hile the 30.9 mile distance is on the shorter side for an endurance race\,
  don't fool yourself into thinking this is going to be a walk in the park.
  You will be served up a heaping helping of elevation gain\, climbing 4874
  feet and descending an equal amount over fast and technical chunky terrai
 n as well as some super omega flow. There will be two rest areas along the
  way (Mile 13 and 23.5) stocked with plenty of water and snacks. The Old F
 ort Fifty will be open to cyclists AND runners! Starting and finishing at 
 Camp Grier\, racers will first head over to the Gateway Trail System\, an 
 inc\n\nMore: http://www.BikeReg.com/old-fort-fifty-2027\n\nSource: BikeReg
 \n\nListed by Altar Cycles — altar.bike/calendar
GEO:35.6462044;-82.1927674
LOCATION:985 Camp Grier Rd\, Old Fort\, NC
URL:http://www.BikeReg.com/old-fort-fifty-2027
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Pisgah Enduro
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270815
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270815
DTSTAMP:20261126T190045Z
UID:903f0caa2f7afb82@altar.bike
CATEGORIES:race
DESCRIPTION:High-speed East Coast technical rocky rooty singletrack ENDURO
  racing in Pisgah National Forest\, around Old Fort\, along the steep esca
 rpment of the Blue Ridge Mountains. With dizzying vertical descents to qua
 d-crushing climbs\, you will ride a roller coaster that puts this region o
 n the map for the downhill minded. The venue is an actual Summer Camp. The
 re’s a lake\, pump track\, post-race cookout\, and more! Choose bunkhous
 e or car/tent camping and spend the weekend racing and enjoying life! The 
 course starts in the shadow of the highest peak East of the Mississippi \,
  Mount Mitchell\, on the legendary Heartbreak Ridge trail. Stage one and t
 wo drop over 3000' elevation in a combined 4.5 miles. Stage three follows 
 with the most amazing trail that parallels Interstate 40… Kitsuma\, and 
 descends an\n\nMore: http://www.BikeReg.com/pisgah-enduro-2027\n\nSource: 
 BikeReg\n\nListed by Altar Cycles — altar.bike/calendar
GEO:35.646372;-82.192121
LOCATION:985 Camp Grier Rd\, Old Fort\, NC
URL:http://www.BikeReg.com/pisgah-enduro-2027
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Gravel Roll - The Holler in Walhalla
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270821
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270821
DTSTAMP:20261126T190045Z
UID:578d116d110cb6d2@altar.bike
CATEGORIES:race
DESCRIPTION:The Gravel Roll is Hollerin' for more in Walhalla in 2027! Gua
 ranteed to make you whoop\, The Holler in Walhalla is our mountain gravel 
 race for the Gravel Roll series. Now in its third ever\, fourth annual edi
 tion! The road surface composition is very similar and is representative o
 f what mountain gravel with the U.S. Forest Service road system is like. T
 here'll be some smooth crush\, some chunky\, and of course a dash of our u
 sual Gravel Roll fun. Like for you Bosses out there\, we've got a little 
 “bonus” for y'all. Like most of our mountain gravel rides\, this one d
 oesn't meet our usual 70% threshold for paved to unpaved\, but we think yo
 u'll welcome the smooth but swoopy tarmac when you encounter it\, and rip 
 it all the same. Afterwards\, hang around at the Walhalla Depot for our us
 ual post rid\n\nMore: http://www.BikeReg.com/the-holler\n\nSource: BikeReg
 \n\nListed by Altar Cycles — altar.bike/calendar
GEO:34.762378;-83.0661084
LOCATION:211 S College St\, Walhalla\, SC
URL:http://www.BikeReg.com/the-holler
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Pisgah 111 / 555
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271002
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271002
DTSTAMP:20261126T190045Z
UID:f6fb2bcb9eae90d0@altar.bike
CATEGORIES:race
DESCRIPTION:The Pisgah 111 is the quintessential crusher of a cross-countr
 y endurance MTB race. Racers follow a 65.1 mile course with 10\,200' feet 
 of climbing along the most iconic trails and gravel roads known in Pisgah 
 National Forest. Just peek at the course map and list of trails and you’
 ll immediately get chills just thinking about the epic scenery and terrain
  you’ll encounter. There will be FOUR rest areas (at three locations) fo
 r the Pisgah 111 that will be stocked with water\, food (PB&J\, fruit\, sa
 lty snacks\, sweet snacks\, bars)\, first aid\, and neutral mechanical sup
 port. Riders may send drop bags to each rest area. Be sure to read the inf
 ormation below\, too. The Pisgah 555 will test the strength and endurance 
 of racers by challenging them to complete a 39.7 mile course with 7325' of
  climbing a\n\nMore: http://www.BikeReg.com/pisgah-111-555-2027\n\nSource:
  BikeReg\n\nListed by Altar Cycles — altar.bike/calendar
GEO:35.2843490812761;-82.7255616999077
LOCATION:1276 Pisgah Hwy\, Pisgah Forest\, NC
URL:http://www.BikeReg.com/pisgah-111-555-2027
END:VEVENT
